## Outcome and conditions

Explain the chapter’s Nogales puzzle and compare Spanish extraction with the unsuccessful coercive strategy in Virginia. Define encomienda/mita precisely, connect outside options to land/voice incentives, and distinguish a historical mechanism from an isolated causal effect while interpreting the two maps’ boundaries/units.

Essential criterion components are **C1 Nogales hypothesis and limit, C2 extraction institutions and local legacy, C3 Jamestown incentives and outside options, C4 comparative qualifications and map limits**. Primary finished-note locations: [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#Nogales: the question that motivates the chapter]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#Spanish colonization: creating rules for extraction]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#Why the first Buenos Aires failed while Asunción prospered for conquerors]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#Capturing leaders and appropriating existing organization]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#The Potosí mita and its local legacy]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#Jamestown: why attempts at coercion changed course]].

Instruction and supported practice may use the selected notes. Independent checks are closed-note: show the stated prompt and its supplied data only, with no explanation, model answer, hints, web search, other people, AI help, or solution-bearing figure access before the response. A simple calculator is allowed for arithmetic after the learner states the reasoning; no symbolic or generative tools. If notes, item keys, or matching solutions were accessed, record the exposure and do not call that attempt independent. No timing or confidence threshold replaces a complete answer. Exact population-unit conversion, colonial-history claims beyond this chapter and present Nogales figures are outside scope. Numerical historical details are source descriptions rather than live facts or controlled estimates.

